    "turn_text": "Welcome to Off Message. I'm Isaac over there. Today's guest, North Carolina Senator Tom Tillis. At strange times in the Republican Senate Conference these days, John McCain is proudly on a final mission to pull his party back from Trump and his conference back from furthering the unraveling of an institution he spent 30 years in. Tennessee Senator Bob Corker is teed off with the liberation of a politician who's personally popular among his colleagues and not running for reelection. The even reporters asking all the other senators whether they do in fact believe everything he said, but just haven't spoken it out loud or on the record. The list goes on. Senators don't know what to make of Trump. They can't figure out when the House is going to get itself together. They're worried for both policy and politics sake about not getting anything done. Few are excited about the prospect of Roy Moore from Alabama joining them if he wins in December. And now they're headed into what should be a layup midterm cycle answering questions about whether Mitch McConnell should even be majority leader and looking over their shoulders at what exactly Steve Bannon's up to. All of this was until it's mind when we sat down in his office in Dirksen, the Senate office building, just across the street from the Capitol. Tillis was elected in the 2014 Republican wave, knocking out first term Democrat K. Hagen, but he'd already gained quite a bit of notoriety and fame from his time as Speaker of the North Carolina State Legislature. We had Roy Cooper, the new governor on, a few months ago, and he talked about how upset he is with what's happened to the way the legislature functions and the gerrymandered lines that favor Republicans. But of course, he's a Democrat fighting against all that. Tillis is a man responsible for much of what he's fighting against, getting put in place to begin with. So that's the perspective that he arrived in Washington with, and with which he's looked at what's been going on in the Senate over the last year and how he thinks things should go from here. Before we get started, I want to make sure you've all hit that subscribe button on Apple Podcast or Panoply or whatever you're listening to us on and you've rated us and told a friend. Episodes coming up, a really great conversation with Nancy Pelosi in which we covered everything from her telling her high school model UN club she couldn't hang out with them because she was having dinner with JFK. all the way to what she makes of Donald Trump. Also coming up, Eric Holder, former Defense Secretary William Perry, talking about North Korea and nuclear war, and many, many more. Follow me on Twitter and Facebook at IsaacDovere, email me your thoughts and guest suggestions to Isaacatpolitico.com. And now, my conversation with Tom Tillis. Can we start with a question that has, I feel like, has been bugging me a lot? What is with the H and Tom?",
