    "turn_idx": 64,
    "turn_text": "The only way the idealized view of what Senator McCain's talking about if other people change behavior and actually would participate in that process in earnest. Look, I get it. If I'm Chuck Schumer, I'm calling for regular order because he knows he can use every device possible to have nothing happen. And so that's why it is critically important for our leadership and why I support Mitch and saying, we'll go down that path, but when we know how the movie is going to end, and the only thing that will have happened is we will have lost weeks or months of chamber time, then we're not going to take that bait. So until you see a change in behavior where Senator Schumer and key members of the Monterey conference are willing to come together and say, you know, this, this, This is broadly where we're willing to negotiate. We will negotiate in good faith. We will go into committees and markups, and we won't play all the sort of delay tactics and the things that I've seen over the last three years. To me, it's a very noble purpose, but it doesn't really exhibit any grasp of what's been going on around here in terms of the tactics used by the",
