    "turn_text": "I think that we have to look at term limits of some sort. I'm not of the mind. I would vote for any term limit bill, but I think some are more elegant and less risky than others. I think one thing, if you create real term limits on leadership and chairmanship, that will create a natural turnover because after somebody's aspired to that level, they're less likely to go on the rank and file it. They know that that's where they'll be for the remainder of their tenure. So I think there's a more elegant way of doing it that makes it less likely that the staff and the bureaucrats really become the governing entity, and we just become actors in the show that come and go every 12 years.",
