    "turn_idx": 100,
    "turn_text": "I mean, people can, you know, if you, the people have one of two reasons to come to Congress to make a point or make a difference and make an appoint if all you're doing is taking a position that prevents the vast majority of your colleagues to get something done. Sooner or later, we will all be held accountable for that. So I think it's itself regulating over time. And so I think that I hope that we all recognize the American people expect a result. I've said to a certain amount of criticism that I didn't view last year's election as a conservative mandate, I viewed it as a results mandate. And if we don't produce a result, if people think that it's going to resonate over time, that it's still on principle, but I allowed Obamacare to remain the law of the land. I stood on principle, so I allowed the United States to continue to be one of the highest-taxed countries in the nation. I stood on principle. and therefore didn't allow us to provide the resources to the military. I think all those things over time will have consequences back in their home states. When",
