    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70874.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 128,
    "turn_text": "She better have a lot of votes that she can bring because I actually think there's a lot of structural problems with that. A straight up DACA provision and the year and appropriations bill could be the reason why it's the first appropriations bill I don't vote for. Because you do see some, you can see some folks here who are just trying to run out the clock and then hope that they can get that measure on and threaten government shutdown. So maybe she has a reason to believe that other than her own opinion of the role that she can play in getting a year in deal. But I think that that's a great disservice to the Dreamers. I think it's a great disservice to the issue. And it literally poisons the well for any other future productive discussion around immigration reform. If you want to set back the rest of the discussion, we want to have around immigration reform back about 20 years, then let her be successful with this sort of shove it down people's throats approach.",
